<div class="container-narrow py-12">
  <%- ui.banner({ tone: 'warning', title: 'Draft — not yet reviewed by a lawyer', text: 'This text describes how the service is designed to handle data. It is a working draft for founder and legal review. Items in [square brackets] must be completed before launch, and this notice removed.' }) %>

  <article class="prose-aeo mt-8">
    <h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
    <p>Dot Bd Solutions, 335/Kha, TV Road, East Rampura, Dhaka-1219, Bangladesh (“AEO Corner”) is the controller of the personal data described here. Contact: <a href="mailto:rajib@dotbdsolutions.com">rajib@dotbdsolutions.com</a>.</p>

    <h2>2. What we collect, and why</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="table">
        <caption class="sr-only">Data we collect, why, and for how long</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Data</th><th scope="col">Why</th><th scope="col">How long</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row" class="row-head">Free audit: website address, work email, your marketing-consent choice, IP address</th><td>To run the audit, send your report, limit abuse, and (only if you consent) send related marketing email.</td><td>12 months if you do not become a customer</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row" class="row-head">Account: name, email, organisation, team members and roles</th><td>To provide the service.</td><td>While your account exists, plus 30 days</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row" class="row-head">Brand details, competitors, questions and content drafts you create</th><td>To provide the service. We treat these as confidential.</td><td>While your account exists</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row" class="row-head">Public web pages we read and AI answers we collect</th><td>To produce your scores and reports.</td><td>13 months</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row" class="row-head">Payment details</th><td>Handled only by Stripe (cards) or bKash (taka). We keep a customer or payment reference, the plan, the amount and the transaction ID, never card numbers, bKash numbers or PINs.</td><td>While your account exists, plus the time the law requires us to keep invoices</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row" class="row-head">Connection secrets (for example a WordPress application password)</th><td>To make changes you approve. Stored encrypted and never shown again.</td><td>Until you disconnect or delete your account</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row" class="row-head">Page views and referrer on this site</th><td>To understand how people find and use the site. Collected without cookies or stored identifiers.</td><td>Per our analytics provider’s retention setting</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 id="google-user-data">3. Google user data</h2>
    <p>This section applies only if you choose to connect your Google account to a project. Connecting is optional, and nothing in AEO Corner needs it to work. We never ask for Google sign-in: signing in to AEO Corner does not give us any Google data.</p>
    <h3>What we access</h3>
    <p>When you connect, Google asks you to approve two <strong>read-only</strong> permissions, and we ask for nothing else (no email address, no profile, no ability to change anything):</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> (<code>analytics.readonly</code>): the traffic reports of the Google Analytics 4 property you choose, limited to visits that came from AI answer engines such as ChatGPT, Perplexity, Gemini and Google AI Overviews. We read the date, the traffic source, the landing page address and the number of sessions.</li>
      <li><strong>Google Search Console</strong> (<code>webmasters.readonly</code>): the search performance of the site you choose: the date, the page address, clicks, impressions, click-through rate and average position. We also read the list of properties and sites on your account once, so that you can pick one.</li>
    </ul>
    <h3>How we use it</h3>
    <p>We use this data only to show you, inside your own AEO Corner project, how much traffic AI answer engines send to your website and how it changes after you make a fix. We do not use it for advertising, we do not build profiles, we do not use it to train artificial-intelligence or machine-learning models, and no person at AEO Corner reads it except to support you when you ask.</p>
    <h3>Who we share it with</h3>
    <p>We do not sell it and we do not share it with anyone else. Your team members in the same organisation can see it in the project. The cloud and database providers that store our data (see the subprocessors list) hold it on our behalf, encrypted in transit, and may not use it for their own purposes.</p>
    <h3>How it is stored and protected</h3>
    <p>The access token Google gives us is stored encrypted, in a separate key-protected form, and is opened only by the background process that reads your reports. The weekly traffic figures we read are stored in our database, kept apart from other organisations’ data.</p>
    <h3>How long we keep it, and how to remove it</h3>
    <p>You can disconnect at any time from the project’s Google connection screen: our copy of the access token is then erased and we stop reading your reports. You can also remove AEO Corner’s access yourself at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" rel="noopener noreferrer">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>. The traffic figures already stored are kept while your account exists and are deleted when your account is deleted; email us at the address in section 8 and we will delete them sooner on request.</p>
    <h3>Google API Services User Data Policy</h3>
    <p>AEO Corner’s use and transfer to any other app of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.</p>

    <h2>4. Marketing email</h2>
    <p>Receiving your audit report does not sign you up for marketing. We send marketing email only if you tick the separate consent box, and every message has an unsubscribe link.</p>

    <h2>5. Cookies</h2>
    <p>This public site does not set cookies of its own and does not use cookie-based analytics. The bot check on our audit form (Cloudflare Turnstile) and our sign-in provider (Clerk) may set strictly necessary cookies to do their job.</p>

    <h2>6. Who we share data with</h2>
    <p>We do not sell personal data, and we do not share Google user data (section 3). We share personal data with the companies below only as needed to run the service.</p>
    <h3 id="subprocessors">Subprocessors</h3>
    <p>The same list, with where each company processes data, is on the <a href="/subprocessors">subprocessors page</a>. We tell customers 30 days before we add one.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="table">
        <caption class="sr-only">Subprocessors</caption>
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Company</th><th scope="col">Purpose</th><th scope="col">Data involved</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <% for (const s of subprocessors.filter((x) => x.status === 'in_use')) { %>
          <tr><th scope="row" class="row-head"><%= s.name %></th><td><%= s.purpose %></td><td><%= s.data %></td></tr>
          <% } %>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>7. Where data is stored</h2>
    <p>Data is stored in the United States. [International transfer mechanism to be completed by counsel.]</p>

    <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask us to access, correct, export or delete your personal data, and to stop marketing email. We act on requests within 30 days. Email <a href="mailto:rajib@dotbdsolutions.com">rajib@dotbdsolutions.com</a>. If you are in the EU, UK or California you may have additional rights, and you can complain to your local data-protection authority.</p>

    <h2>9. Security</h2>
    <p>Data is encrypted in transit, secrets are encrypted at rest, and each organisation’s data is kept separate from others’. No system is perfectly secure; if a breach affects you we will tell you as the law requires.</p>

    <h2>10. Children</h2>
    <p>AEO Corner is for businesses and is not directed at children.</p>

    <h2>11. Changes</h2>
    <p>If we change this policy in a way that matters, we will tell you before it takes effect.</p>
  </article>
